I fixed `parseTags()` in `src/tags.ts`. It now trims and lowercases each tag, drops empty ones, and removes repeats while keeping each tag where it first appeared. `' Red, blue ,red,, '` now gives `['red', 'blue']`.

```ts
export function parseTags(text: string): string[] {
  const tags = text.split(",").map((tag) => tag.trim().toLowerCase());
  // A Set keeps insertion order, so each tag stays where it first appeared.
  return [...new Set(tags.filter((tag) => tag !== ""))];
}
```

